    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "id": "H01",
        "hypothesis": "ROOT CAUSE: deploy dep-8841's retry change (retrying POST on 503, no backoff, up to 4 attempts) combined with the design that holds the DB connection across the payment call. Together they turned a short third-party gateway 503 burst into DB pool exhaustion (15/15) on checkout-api-3. That caused 10s pool-timeout 503s on all endpoints, including /cart and /orders. Under the previous config, POST charges would have failed fast on the first 503, releasing connections, and the damage would have been limited to the gateway-failed checkouts. Remediation: roll back with kubectl rollout undo, or restore allowed_methods to idempotent verbs, add backoff, and cap the total retry time. Longer term, release the DB connection before the external call and add idempotency keys before retrying any POST charge.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "supporting_evidence": "Diff and runbook (S01). Gateway burst from 09:19:37 to 09:21:09 (S09, S03). Retried POSTs holding connections for 7\u201331s (S16, S12, S11). Pool at 15/15 from 09:19:50 to 09:21:00 (S02). 105 pool-timeout 503s vs 19 gateway 503s, with 68 of the pool timeouts on non-payment GETs (S15, S10). The checkout 5xx window matches pool saturation (S05). Alternatives ruled out: S13, S14, S04. Caveat: there is no pre-deploy gateway burst to compare against, so the counterfactual (old config would not have exhausted the pool) is inferred from the docs and the diff, and should be tested in replay.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S01",
          "S02",
          "S03",
          "S05",
          "S09",
          "S10",
          "S11",
          "S12",
          "S15",
          "S16"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "documentation": [
      {
        "id": "D01",
        "url": "https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/urllib3.util.html",
        "claim": "urllib3 Retry: allowed_methods defaults to idempotent verbs only; \"Set to a None value to retry on any verb\". A status_forcelist retry happens only if the request method is in allowed_methods. Under the old config (allowed_methods={\"GET\"}), POST /v1/charges 503s would not have been retried. Under the new config (None, with 503 in forcelist and backoff 0), they are. This is documented behavior, not incident evidence."
      }
    ],
